<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">20042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>US forces have seized an Iranian cargo ship in the Strait of Hormuz, and Tehran's responded by rejecting the second round of peace talks Pakistan was set to host on Tuesday.</s> <s>Wednesday's ceasefire deadline now expires with no deal, the blockade enforced by boarding actions, and Iran calling the seizure an act of war.</s> <s>Uranium enrichment and maritime sovereignty remain the disputes nobody's been able to bridge.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Spain's prime minister will propose Tuesday that the European Union scrap its Association Agreement with Israel, the framework governing forty-five billion euros in annual trade and binding both parties to a human rights clause.</s> <s>The agreement's been in force since the year two thousand, and the European Commission itself has found Israel may be in breach.</s> <s>The proposal needs a qualified majority at the Council, where Germany and Hungary have so far blocked any move with teeth.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bulgaria's progressive anti-corruption bloc won thirty-nine percent in Sunday's snap election, projecting one hundred eleven seats... ten short of a governing majority.</s> <s>The country's held successive snap votes since two thousand twenty-one as fragmented parliaments collapsed one after another.</s> <s>Coalition talks now decide whether reformers can finally cross the threshold or whether Sofia returns to the polls again.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The British Foreign Office overruled Peter Mandelson's failed security vetting before appointing him ambassador to Washington, and Prime Minister Starmer says he learned of that power only this week.</s> <s>Government rules permitted the override, but Starmer's account that he didn't know faces a test on Tuesday.</s> <s>Former Foreign Office chief Olly Robins testifies to parliament that day, and his version could contradict the prime minister directly.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Africa's National Prosecuting Authority let the Swiss multinational ABB pay two and a half billion rand to escape prosecution over corruption at the Kusile power station.</s> <s>The settlement leaned on a US conviction already on record, while a former Eskom executive facing his own trial argues this creates two-tier justice... corporations buy reparations, individuals get courtrooms.</s> <s>A high court hears that challenge on Monday, and a ruling against the deal could void the immunity entirely.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The United Arab Emirates has quietly asked the US Federal Reserve for a currency swap line, fearing war could drain reserves and trigger capital flight from the dirham.</s> <s>The central bank governor raised the proposal in Washington last week, with no formal request yet filed and twenty-eight hundred missiles already struck in the conflict.</s> <s>Abu Dhabi's posture of staying clear of the war is collapsing into open financial dependence on Washington.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's tariffs on finished imported goods have climbed to seventy percent, what the Centre for the Promotion of Private Enterprise calls structured industrialisation.</s> <s>The same group warned that import-reliant businesses face severe cost shocks, and Nigerian petroleum refiners with recent investment got no protection at all.</s> <s>Abuja's bet is that domestic production catches up before consumers run out of patience.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A single accounting bug in the Kelp restaking bridge let attackers mint two hundred ninety-two million dollars of unbacked synthetic tokens, then borrow real assets against them on Aave.</s> <s>Aave's left holding collateral it can't sell, and Ledger's chief technology officer says twenty twenty-six is on track to be decentralised finance's worst year ever for hacks.</s> <s>The structural problem is that composability — the feature these protocols sell — has become the attack surface no audit can keep pace with.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's foreign secretary told Colombo the Trincomalee energy hub can't wait, pressing Sri Lanka to operationalise the deep-water port that bypasses Hormuz entirely.</s> <s>The site holds a colonial-era complex of ninety-nine fuel storage tanks, only fourteen of which are currently in use.</s> <s>Fuel prices across South Asia rose after February's war, and New Delhi wants the hub running before the next disruption arrives.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India is also relaxing the twenty twenty restrictions it placed on Chinese investment after the Galwan border clash, rules that required government approval for every Chinese direct investment.</s> <s>New Delhi's testing whether eased terms draw Chinese capital away from rival destinations in Southeast Asia.</s> <s>The geopolitical signal cuts against Washington's effort to corral allies into a single posture toward Beijing.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A new study finds that slag activated with sodium carbonate gains ten to twelve percent strength over ninety days and matches Portland cement, which generates eight percent of global carbon dioxide emissions on its own.</s> <s>The activators are non-corrosive, and the precursor is industrial waste from steelmaking that's already piling up.</s> <s>Researchers say the bottleneck to replacing Portland isn't the chemistry... it's building codes that haven't caught up.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Japan's XRISM satellite has measured X-ray spectra from the Perseus Cluster that break the standard models for Type-Ia supernovae.</s> <s>The abundances of chromium, manganese, and nickel in the intracluster gas don't match what white-dwarf detonations should produce, forcing a rethink of the chemistry behind these explosions.</s> <s>Revised yields would shift estimates of stellar ages and the timeline of the universe's chemical evolution.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers have built synthetic cells that generate mechanical force on command, adding light-triggered contractile elements to artificial cells already equipped with membranes and metabolism.</s> <s>It's a step toward synthetic biology that doesn't just sit in a dish but moves, divides, and delivers cargo.</s> <s>Drug delivery and artificial cell division remain lab-stage proofs of concept for now.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Germany's chancellor Friedrich Merz used the Hannover Messe stage to demand Brussels carve industrial artificial intelligence out of the EU AI Act entirely, covering predictive maintenance, robotics, and factory-floor models.</s> <s>Berlin plans to quadruple its national AI investment alongside the request, the first major G-seven leader to publicly call for rolling back Europe's signature tech regulation.</s> <s>The regulatory moat the EU spent years building is now being breached from inside by its largest economy.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Moscow's mobile internet was shut for three weeks while authorities banned virtual private networks, instituted whitelists of approved sites, and blocked Telegram outright.</s> <s>State media justified the lockdown by citing US strikes on Iran, and the Kremlin announced a national artificial intelligence project in the same breath.</s> <s>What Russia's calling AI sovereignty looks operationally like the most aggressive internet shutdown a major economy has yet attempted.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Istanbul, the lira's collapse has made dollar-denominated cloud computing unaffordable, and developers are migrating en masse to European dedicated servers.</s> <s>A Hetzner box that costs two hundred thirty-three dollars matches a DigitalOcean server billed at fourteen hundred thirty-two, a six-fold gap that holds for steady workloads.</s> <s>The hyperscaler premium only pays off where managed services are actively used, and most workloads simply aren't.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>